Design references (no code copied)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following open-source projects were studied while designing specific
modules. The in-tree implementations are independent (different language or
different abstraction level). The entries record the inspiration so a
reviewer can compare upstream and in-tree; the per-module detail is in
PROVENANCE_NOTES.md.

JustVugg/colibri
    https://github.com/JustVugg/colibri
    Copyright the colibri contributors
    Licensed under Apache-2.0

    On-device mixture-of-experts inference engine. Its core design, a
    placement hierarchy across VRAM, RAM and disk for expert weights,
    influenced the weight-residency planner in
    crates/ai-inference/crates/ai-serve/src/residency.rs (tier model and the
    invariant that placement must never change semantics). No code was
    copied: colibri is a pure C runtime, and the in-tree module is a Rust
    planner that explicitly contains none of colibri's runtime machinery.

1jehuang/jcode
    https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode
    Copyright the jcode contributors
    Licensed under MIT

    Coding agent studied for its memory discipline. The bounded-buffer and
    ceiling behaviour it prompted is ours and is described in
    docs/ARCHITECTURE.md. No code was copied.

A corpus of published system prompts (consulted while writing
crates/ai-inference/crates/ai-core/src/system_prompt.rs; the corpus is not
redistributed and no single upstream repository is named here).
    The consultation covered prompt structure only. The in-tree prompt is
    original text: it states this protocol's own limits and is checked
    against the tree by the ai-inference-prompt-is-true gate. No prompt
    text was reproduced.

